        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep read warning args previews UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `read` tool validation warning preview must be both UTF-16 safe and visibly truncated when raw string args exceed the warning preview budget. The first safe-slice fix avoided split surrogate output, but at an emoji boundary it could shrink the raw prefix to exactly the final preview limit and accidentally drop the existing ellipsis marker.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe follow-up keeps an explicit `wasRawTruncated` signal before sanitization. If the raw args exceeded the warning preview budget and the sanitized safe prefix did not already include the truncation marker, the warning preview appends the existing ellipsis marker while still avoiding lone surrogate output.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRead-tool validation warnings and console diagnostics stay well-formed at emoji/astral boundaries and still visibly indicate that oversized args were truncated.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact reviewed head after bot follow-up: `1e6f0ab0fa0`\n- `git diff --check`: pass\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts`: pass\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxlint src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts`: pass\n- Production-handler proof with `node --import tsx --input-type=module` calling `handleToolExecutionStart` for `read` args shaped as `200 x chars + U+1F600 + tail`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"event\": \"embedded_read_tool_start_warning\",\n  \"codePoints\": 201,\n  \"lastCodePointHex\": \"2026\",\n  \"ellipsisPreserved\": true,\n  \"containsEmoji\": false,\n  \"loneSurrogate\": false,\n  \"consoleMessageTail\": \"xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx?\"\n}\n```\n\n- Regression coverage now expects both oversized ASCII args and the emoji-boundary args path to retain the truncation marker without producing lone surrogates.\n\nKnown proof gap: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts -- --testNamePattern \"read warning args\"` did not return output before the local 180s timeout in this Windows worktree, so the current update does not claim a fresh local Vitest pass. CI should provide the full test signal for the pushed head.\n",
        "branch": "codex/read-tool-args-preview-utf16",
